    "description": "Thin-wake rigidity derives the standard layer profile and all longitudinal residues from full drift (2,-2), growth twelve, width ten and at most one odd class on each interior level. General non-axis wake budgets and inverse synthesis remain. A mixed-wake interleaving parity identity gives an arbitrary-width necessary screen at full drift (2,-2); attributed periodic-growth dependencies and the separate profile-classification replay are retained. A quadratic wake character now covers every non-axis full drift, with compressed polynomial-bit evaluation and an unbounded growth-eight exclusion family. A purely analytic unit-diagonal proof and thin-profile parity pruning are integrated.",
